  "releaseNotes": "2.2.0: BREAKING. Default problem schemas are now CoreProblemDetails (replaces ProblemDetails)\n\t\t\tand CoreValidationProblemDetails (replaces ValidationProblemDetails for the 400 response).\n\t\t\tOpenApiProblemResponsesOptions.SchemaId defaults to CoreProblemDetails, ProblemSchemaIds\n\t\t\tincludes CoreProblemDetails by default. The new ValidationSchemaId property controls the\n\t\t\t400 schema; when it is not set, the 400 schema is CoreValidationProblemDetails while SchemaId\n\t\t\tkeeps its default, and follows SchemaId otherwise. To restore the previous schema names, set SchemaId = \"ProblemDetails\" and\n\t\t\tValidationSchemaId = \"ValidationProblemDetails\", and keep both names in ProblemSchemaIds.\n\t\t\tConsumers that reference ProblemDetails or ValidationProblemDetails in generated clients must\n\t\t\tupdate those references.\n\t\t\t2.1.0: Added ProducesConflictProblemAttribute (HTTP 409) for documenting conflict\n\t\t\tproblem responses. Minor version bump.",
